d head not in current:\n    bad.append(f\"orphan entry {o['seq']}: the attested head {head} was published on {a.git_rev} and later removed\")\n    continue\n```\n\nI should add:\n```python\nproblem = _orphan_entries_problem(o, pred)\nif problem:\n    bad.append(f\"orphan entry {o['seq']}: hidden entries problem: {problem}\")\n    continue\n```\n\nBut wait, `o` is the orphan entry from the chain. Let me check the structure:\n```python\nexplained = {e[\"body\"][\"log_index\"]: e for e, _ in chain if e[\"kind\"] == \"orphan\"}\n...\no = explained[idx]\n```\nSo `o` is the full orphan entry (with `seq`, `prev`, `kind`, `written_at`, `body`). And `o[\"body\"]` has `entries_b64`.\n\nActually, looking at the function signature: `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict)`. The `orphan` parameter should be the orphan's body, or the full orphan entry? The task says `orphan[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]`, so `orphan` is the full orphan entry dict.\n\nLet me implement this now.\n\nAlso, I need to add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields in `check_body` for orphan kind.\n\nLet me start editing the file.",
