          "type": "thinking",
          "thinking": "The implementation is complete. Let me summarize what was done:\n\n1. Added `entries_b64` to the allowed fields for orphan entries in `check_body()` (line 152)\n2. Added schema validation for `entries_b64` - must be a list of base64 strings (lines 159-168)\n3. Added the `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None` function (lines 304-345) that:\n   - Returns `None` when the decoded entries exactly match the attested range\n   - Returns a string containing \"range\" when the count is wrong\n   - Returns a string containing \"chain\" when an entry's `prev` doesn't link correctly\n   - Returns a string containing \"head\" when the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`\n4. Wired the function into `cmd_monitor()` (lines 594-597) so that orphans without valid hidden entries are reported as \"wrong\"\n\nAll existing tests pass.",
